hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21553","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy ibn Damrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that a man vaunted with the vaunt of Jahiliyyah, so he made him bite, and did not use a euphemism. The people looked at him. He said to the people: I see what is in your selves. I could not but say this. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us: When you hear one who vaunts with the vaunt of Jahiliyyah, make him bite, and do not use euphemism."
"21554","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: I saw a man vaunting by Ubayy with the vaunt of Jahiliyyah, boasting of his father, so he made him bite his father, and did not use euphemism. Then he said to them: I see what is in your selves. I cannot but do that. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever vaunts with the vaunt of Jahiliyyah, make him bite, and do not use euphemism."
"21555","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, from Ubayy, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"21556","Isma'il narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, that a man vaunted with the vaunt of Jahiliyyah, and he mentioned the hadith. Ubayy said: We were commanded, when a man vaunts with the vaunt of Jahiliyyah, to make him bite his father's hen, and not use euphemism."
"21557","Abdullah narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar ibn Maysarah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, he said: Ubayy said: We were commanded, when a man vaunts, and he mentioned the like of it."
"21558","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa al-'Anazi narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, from Ubayy, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: For ablution there is a devil called al-Walahan, so beware of him, or he said: So be cautious of him."
"21559","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The food of the son of Adam is made an example of the world. Even if he seasons it and salts it, look to what it becomes."
"21560","Abdullah narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, he said: I saw an old man in Madinah speaking, and I asked about him. They said: This is Ubayy ibn Ka'b. He said: Adam, peace be upon him, when death came to him, said to his sons: O my sons, I desire of the fruits of Paradise. So they went seeking for him. The angels met them, with them his shrouds and his embalming, and with them axes, and spades, and baskets. They said to them: O sons of Adam, what do you want, and what do you seek, or: What do you want, and where are you going? They said: Our father is sick, and he desired of the fruits of Paradise. They said to them: Return, for the decree of your father has been decreed. So they came. When Hawwa' saw them, she recognized them, so she clung to Adam. He said: Away from me, away from me, for I was only afflicted from your side. Leave between me and the angels of my Lord, Blessed and Exalted. So they took his soul, and washed him, and shrouded him, and embalmed him, and dug for him, and made a niche for him, and prayed over him. Then they entered his grave, and placed him in his grave, and placed bricks over him. Then they came out of the grave, then threw soil over him. Then they said: O sons of Adam, this is your sunnah."
